Recursive descent parsing is a top-down parsing technique where each non-terminal in the grammar has a corresponding recursive function. The parser starts from the start symbol and tries to derive the input string.

Example for grammar: E → T + E | T, T → id

Function parseE() {
  parseT();
  if (lookahead == '+') {
    match('+');
    parseE();
  }
}

Function parseT() {
  if (lookahead == 'id') {
    match('id');
  } else error();
}

Advantages: Simple to implement, good error messages.
Disadvantages: May require backtracking, left recursion must be eliminated.
